cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CytoNucs: Hierarchical Instance Segmentation in 2D and 3D with StarDist-Guided Mask Refinement"
authors:
  - family-names: Maiurov
    given-names: Miroslav
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5935-6452"
  - family-names: Horváth
    given-names: Péter
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4492-1798"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/podtyazhki1337/Cyto-Nucs-Stardist-2D-3D"
url: "https://huggingface.co/Podtyazhki1337/cytonucs"
keywords:
  - hierarchical instance segmentation
  - nested objects
  - StarDist
  - promptable segmentation
  - nucleus and cell segmentation
  - 3D microscopy
  - computed tomography
abstract: >-
  CytoNucs segments objects that lie inside other objects (nuclei inside cells, nucleoli inside nuclei, renal masses
  inside kidneys) in 2D images and 3D volumes and links every child to its parent. A shared network generates
  StarDist object proposals whose locations and extents define prompts for jointly trained mask refinement branches;
  each child prompt predicts masks for both the child and its parent.
